dup  ( a -- a a )
  context: ~   source: src/reva.f
  Duplicate the top stack item
see  ( <name> -- )
  context: ~util   source: src/reva.f
  Dumps the bytes corresponding to the "xt" of "<name>".

  If the library 'debugger' has not been 'need'ed yet, will do a
  dump of the bytes corresponding to the xt.  If that library has
  been 'need'ed, it will try to disassemble.
notebook  ( -- )
  context: ~   source: lib/ui/notebook
  Opens a small notebook in the TUI: type Forth lines in the top pane;
  Ctrl-J or F6 evaluates the line under the cursor and shows what it
  printed, any error and the stack it left in the lower pane.  F1 shows the
  keys.  Done or the close box closes it; its text is kept in notebook.txt.
needs  ( <name> -- )
  context: ~   source: src/reva.f
  Locates the file "<name>" in the user library directory or the
  standard library directory includes it if it has not already been
  included.
no help for nosuchword
notebook 
help WORD    the documentation of WORD (help dup, help notebook)
help/ TEXT   the documented words whose names contain TEXT
